-- §8 I4 — A SIGNATURE `=>` CONSTRAINT NAMES ITS OWN CLASS, NOT A SAME-SPELLED
-- FOREIGN ONE.  This is #1438's OWN repro, moved here verbatim when U1b (#1482)
-- drained its `must_fail` pin: the pin asserted the bug still reproduced, and it
-- does not any more, so the S0 needs a POSITIVE guard or it has none at all.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER, HAND-DERIVED FROM DICT-SEMANTICS §3 + §8 I4, not read off a binary:
--   1. `zmod` declares its own `interface Sizer a where bulk` and, in the SAME
--      module, `useBulk : Sizer b => b -> Int`.  Exactly one `Sizer` is in scope
--      there (§8 I4 qualification 1: a same-module declaration wins over an
--      import — and `zmod` imports nothing at all), so the `=>` occurrence
--      unambiguously denotes `zmod.Sizer`, identity `(zmod, Sizer)`.
--   2. `main` calls `useBulk 3`, instantiating `b := Int`, which poses the goal
--      `zmod.Sizer Int`.
--   3. `match(IE, zmod.Sizer Int)` is EMPTY.  The graph's only `impl Sizer Int`
--      belongs to `amod.Sizer` — a different declaration whose method set
--      (`weight`) is disjoint from `zmod.Sizer`'s (`bulk`).  An impl of one class
--      is not an impl of another that merely shares a spelling.
--   ⇒ REJECT, `No impl of Sizer for Int` (`T-NO-IMPL`), on all three verbs.
--      There is no value to pin: the program never runs.
--
-- 🚨 WHAT THIS ROW GUARDS, MEASURED ON A `main`-BUILT BINARY (709db738) BEFORE
-- U1b: this exact program was a SILENT ACCEPT — `check` exit 0 printing
-- `main : Unit`; `run` E-PANIC `unbound identifier: bulk` (the dict-passing
-- machinery handed `useBulk` a dictionary shaped for `amod.Sizer`, i.e.
-- `{weight}`, and projecting `bulk` out of it found nothing); `build` exit 0 with
-- a binary that SEGFAULTS at 139.  That was #1438.  If a later change re-widens
-- the SIGNATURE-CONSTRAINT channel back to a spelling, THIS ROW GOES
-- GREEN-BY-ACCEPTING and the S0 is back — which is exactly what it exists to stop.
--
-- ⚠️ TOPOLOGICALLY DISCRIMINATING BY CONSTRUCTION, which is not automatic here.
-- The goal is posed by `zmod`'s signature and elaborated when `zmod` is
-- processed; `amod`'s foreign impl lives in a module `zmod` does not import.  A
-- shape whose goal is posed only in `main` would be a false null, because `main`
-- is always topologically LAST and therefore always sees the whole universe.
--
-- ⚠️ Distinct from `i4-xmod-requires-foreign-iface-rejected` (the sibling row):
-- that one reaches the collision through an impl's `requires` (`requireOrigin`),
-- a channel #1446/PR #1480 already gave identity.  THIS one reaches it through a
-- constrained binding's `=>` slot re-instantiated at a CROSS-MODULE call site —
-- `funConstraintIfacesRef` + `schemeObligationsRef`, the two tables U1b widened.
-- The two rows are the same S0 through two different producers, and before U1b
-- exactly one of them rejected.
import amod
import zmod.{useBulk}

main = println (useBulk 3)
